Id: foyer_flower_vase
Name: Flower Vase
Prototype: item
Container: foyer_table
Tags: foyer_vase
Rarity: common
DescriptionShort: A teal {{ e.name }} with yellow roses in it
DescriptionLong: a teal ceramic vase with gold trim around the lip. A couple yellow roses sit inside.
OnAttack: {{ effects.grant_xp("attack", 25) }}{{ effects.destroy() }}{{ effects.broadcast("**" ~ user ~ "** smashes the " ~ e.name ~ "!") }}You momentarily give in to your impulses and strike the {{ e.name }} as hard as you can with your fist. Shards of teal ceramic scatter across the floor. Among the debris, you notice something...{{ effects.grant_random("foyer_vase_loot") }}

Id: foyer_yellow_rose
Name: Yellow Rose
Prototype: item
Tags: foyer_vase_loot
Rarity: common
DescriptionShort: a {{ e.name }}
DescriptionLong: A single yellow rose, slightly crushed but still vibrant.
OnTouch: You gently touch the petals, they are soft. You touch the stem, it's thorny. You can't figure out if you are an optimist or a pessimist.
OnAttack: {{ effects.grant_xp("attack", 25) }}{{ effects.destroy() }}{{ effects.broadcast("**" ~ user ~ "** drops a " ~ e.name ~ " on the floor and crushes it underfoot") }}You feel animosity towards the rose for some reason.
OnUse: You smell the rose. It smells lovely! You feel a bit better now.

Id: foyer_yellow_rose_exquisite
Name: Exquisite Yellow Rose
Prototype: item
Tags: foyer_vase_loot
Rarity: rare
DescriptionShort: an {{ e.name }}
DescriptionLong: A single yellow rose of uncanny beauty. It looks like something you'd see in a magazine.
OnTouch: You gently stroke the petals, careful not to upset the beautiful symmetry of them. They are soft and slightly cold to the touch. You touch the stem, it's covered in extremely sharp thorns. The thorns are there to protect the beautiful flower from being picked, but I guess they failed.
OnAttack: {{ effects.grant_xp("attack", 100) }}{{ effects.destroy() }}{{ effects.broadcast("**" ~ user ~ "** drops an " ~ e.name ~ " on the floor and crushes it underfoot") }}You feel like you have to destroy something beautiful.
OnUse: You smell the rose. It reminds you of an expensive perfume but way more pleasant. You feel better now.

Id: foyer_plaque
Name: Inscribed Plaque
Prototype: object
Room: foyer
Container: foyer_table
DescriptionShort: An {{ e.name }}
DescriptionLong: A wooden plaque with a shiny brass plate. The inscription reads: "Welcome to my mansion! You can usually find us in the office down the hall. -Frizzle"

Id: foyer_note
Name: Handwritten Note
Prototype: item
Tags: foyer_note
Container: foyer_table
Rarity: quest
DescriptionShort: A {{ e.name }} rests on the table
DescriptionLong: A crumpled piece of paper with scribbled instructions. It reads:
+> "Hey! New here? The **/interact** command is your friend! Use it like **/interact** with:**item** action:**verb**. For example: **/interact Treasure take** or **/interact Crate open**.\
 Try experimenting with different verbs to get surprising results. Most items respond to the same basic actions, you'll figure it out!"
OnTouch: You run your fingers over the crumpled paper. The ink is slightly smudged, as if someone wrote it in a hurry. It feels like regular notebook paper. Try to __use__ it for something?
OnAttack: {{ effects.grant_xp("attack", 25) }}{{ effects.destroy() }}{{ effects.broadcast("**" ~ user ~ "** tears up " ~ e ~ "!") }}You crumple the {{ e.name }} into a tiny ball and tear it to shreds. The paper confetti scatters across the table. Well, that's one way to interact with it! You could have also tried __opening__ it or __taking__ it, but destruction works too.
OnUse: You flip the {{ e.name }} over, looking for more information. The back is blank except for a small doodle of a smiling face. Not particularly useful, but cute! Have you tried __opening__ it or __taking__ it yet?
OnTake: {{ effects.pickup() }}{{ effects.broadcast(user ~ " pockets " ~ e ~ ".") }}You fold the {{ e.name }} and tuck it into your pocket. Now you have a handy reference! Most items in the mansion respond to common verbs like look, touch, attack, use, take, open, close, and drop. Try __dropping__ it later to put it back.
OnOpen: You unfold the {{ e.name }} and flatten it out on the table. The creases make it a bit easier to read now. It's the same instructions about /interact, but now you can see a small footnote: "P.S. - Try __closing__ things after you __open__ them. Some containers have surprises inside!"
OnClose: You carefully fold the {{ e.name }} back into a neat square. It's more compact now, though still readable. You've discovered that most items have consistent interactions - this note responds to almost everything! Try __taking__ it with you, or maybe __attack__ it if you're feeling destructive?
OnDrop: {% if container %}You place the {{ e.name }} back on the *{{ container.name }}*.{% else %}You set the {{ e.name }} down on the table.{% endif %}{{ effects.drop() }}{{ effects.broadcast(user ~ " places " ~ e ~ " back down.") }}And that's the /interact command in action! You've successfully experimented with multiple verbs. Keep exploring the mansion - there's a lot to discover!

