Id: terminal_inbox_kickoff
Name: INBOX - Project Kickoff
Prototype: terminal_document
Room: office
Container: office_terminal
DescriptionLong: ```
+ FROM: frizzle@mudd.local
+ TO: team@mudd.local
+ SUBJECT: Project Kickoff
+ DATE: 2025-12-29
+ ----------------------------------------
+
+ The Discord MUD is officially underway.
+
+ The idea: use Discord channels as physical rooms. Players can only
+ see the channel they're currently in - "fog of war" via permissions.
+
+ Movement, exploration, entities coming up next
+
+ -Frizzle
+ ```

Id: terminal_inbox_movement
Name: INBOX - We Have Movement!
Prototype: terminal_document
Room: office
Container: office_terminal
DescriptionLong: ```
+ FROM: frizzle@mudd.local
+ TO: team@mudd.local
+ SUBJECT: We Have Movement!
+ DATE: 2025-12-30
+ ----------------------------------------
+
+ /move now hides the old channel and reveals the new one.
+ You can actually explore the mansion now without seeing
+ everything at once.
+ 
+ Discord's UI hates the idea of yanking permissions from users and refuses to redraw the UI.
+ So I had to have users click on the channel name in the movement message. It's not a deal breaker.
+
+ -Frizzle
+ ```

Id: terminal_inbox_entities
Name: INBOX - Entities Are Alive
Prototype: terminal_document
Room: office
Container: office_terminal
DescriptionLong: ```
+ FROM: frizzle@mudd.local
+ TO: team@mudd.local
+ SUBJECT: Entities Are Alive
+ DATE: 2026-01-14
+ ----------------------------------------
+
+ I implemented a prototype based entity system so we can start filling rooms with stuff.
+ I'm starting with just static entities for now. Later I'll add dynamic spawning and destroyable entities etc.
+
+ /look now shows what's in the room. Tables, vases, furniture.
+ /interact lets you poke things. Jinja templates for responses.
+
+ -Frizzle
+ ```

Id: terminal_inbox_loot
Name: INBOX - Inventory and Loot
Prototype: terminal_document
Room: office
Container: office_terminal
DescriptionLong: ```
+ FROM: frizzle@mudd.local
+ TO: team@mudd.local
+ SUBJECT: Inventory and Loot
+ DATE: 2026-01-25
+ ----------------------------------------
+
+ (update as of 16436296f13f91bde99f1568d32e8ba2f11cea38)
+
+ I added an inventory system that gives each user a unique forum channel where all their items are modeled as threads.
+ Users can interact with the items in the item's thead.
+
+ So players can pick stuff up, drop things, destroy things.
+
+ Spawning pools, rarity tiers, scripted item grants.
+ The whole item lifecycle is done.
+
+ Next up is adding dumb stuff like slot machines, fishing, clay pots to smash.
+ Then I'm thinking we need to add a currency system.
+
+ -Frizzle
+ ```

Id: terminal_inbox_currency
Name: INBOX - Money Makes the World Go Round
Prototype: terminal_document
Room: office
Container: office_terminal
DescriptionLong: ```
+ FROM: frizzle@mudd.local
+ TO: team@mudd.local
+ SUBJECT: Money Makes the World Go Round
+ DATE: 2026-01-27
+ ----------------------------------------
+
+ (update as of 31f1993add6a5ce79186a15b3d18ac3f6e48c0c2)
+
+ Big update! We now have an economy.
+
+ CURRENCY SYSTEM
+ Every player starts with ¥1,000 and gets a wallet pinned in their
+ inventory. Use /pay to send yen to other players in the same room.
+ There's a house account with 1 billion yen that funds all the loot.
+ Double-entry ledger for full auditability.
+
+ SLOT MACHINE
+ Added a one-armed bandit to the lounge. Pull the handle to win prizes!
+ New effects.dispense() transfers random items from containers to your
+ inventory. Prizes include Ring Pops (common to legendary), White Claws,
+ Avatar Blu-rays, and currency pickups.
+
+ CURRENCY PICKUPS
+ New item type that grants yen directly without clogging inventory:
+ - loose_coins: ¥100 (common)
+ - bundle_of_bills: ¥1,000 (uncommon)
+ - money_clip: ¥5,000 (rare)
+ - cash_envelope: ¥25,000 (epic)
+ - briefcase_of_cash: ¥100,000 (legendary)
+ - gold_brick: ¥500,000 (mythic)
+
+ GALLERY
+ The gallery now has a rotating wall of paintings that spawn from
+ a pool. Each is real art from community members. Take them, hang
+ them on the wall, or... destroy them if you're a monster.
+
+ Also added no_duplicates option to spawning pools so the desk
+ drawer and gallery don't spawn the same item twice.
+
+ -Frizzle
+ ```

